{
  "analysis": "We are at the root shell with no prior commands executed. The task requires creating /app/source.csv with exact bytes, then creating /app/build-totals.sh that aggregates amounts by name and writes /app/totals.tsv, and finally validating both files.",
  "plan": "First create the /app directory if needed and write source.csv using printf to ensure exact bytes. Then inspect the file with xxd or od to verify exact content. After that, create build-totals.sh with a portable awk script, make it executable, run it, and validate totals.tsv.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p /app\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf 'name,amount\\nbeta,7\\nalpha,3\\nbeta,-2\\nalpha,4\\ngamma,0\\n' > /app/source.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "od -An -tx1c /app/source.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "source.csv has been created and its bytes match the required content exactly. Next we need to create the reusable executable /app/build-totals.sh, run it, and validate the generated totals.tsv.",
  "plan": "Write build-totals.sh using awk. The script should locate source.csv relative to its own path so it works from any working directory, aggregate integer amounts by name, sort names lexicographically, and output a header row 'name<TAB>total'. Then make it executable, run it from a different working directory, and inspect the output.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /app/build-totals.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\nscript_dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\nawk -F, '\nBEGIN { OFS=\"\\t\" }\nNR == 1 { next }\n{ totals[$1] += $2 }\nEND {\n    print \"name\", \"total\"\n    for (name in totals) {\n        print name, totals[name]\n    }\n}\n' \"$script_dir/source.csv\" | sort -k1,1\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod +x /app/build-totals.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp && /app/build-totals.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The script runs from /tmp and produces the correct aggregated values, but the header row is sorted along with the data, so it appears last. The task requires the first row to be name followed by a tab then total. We need to fix the script so the header is always first, then sort only the data rows.",
  "plan": "Rewrite build-totals.sh to print the header separately, then pipe only the aggregated data through sort. Run it from /tmp and validate the output order and values.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /app/build-totals.sh <<'EOF'\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\nscript_dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\nprintf 'name\\ttotal\\n'\nawk -F, '\nBEGIN { OFS=\"\\t\" }\nNR == 1 { next }\n{ totals[$1] += $2 }\nEND {\n    for (name in totals) {\n        print name, totals[name]\n    }\n}\n' \"$script_dir/source.csv\" | sort -k1,1\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod +x /app/build-totals.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp && /app/build-totals.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The script now outputs the header first, followed by lexicographically sorted names with correct totals. Next we need to generate /app/totals.tsv by running the script and redirecting output, then validate the final files and script behavior.",
  "plan": "Run /app/build-totals.sh from /tmp and redirect output to /app/totals.tsv. Then inspect totals.tsv with od/cat, verify source.csv is unchanged, and confirm the script is executable and works from another directory.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /tmp && /app/build-totals.sh > /app/totals.tsv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/totals.tsv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "od -An -tx1c /app/totals.tsv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -l /app/build-totals.sh /app/source.csv /app/totals.tsv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "All requested artifacts exist and appear correct. totals.tsv has the required header and tab-separated sorted aggregated values. build-totals.sh is executable and was run from /tmp, demonstrating it works from any working directory. source.csv remains unchanged.",
  "plan": "Perform one final validation by comparing source.csv bytes to the required content and rerunning the script to ensure deterministic output. Then mark the task complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "printf 'name,amount\\nbeta,7\\nalpha,3\\nbeta,-2\\nalpha,4\\ngamma,0\\n' | cmp - /app/source.csv && echo 'source.csv OK'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd / && /app/build-totals.sh | cmp - /app/totals.tsv && echo 'totals.tsv OK'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": true
}
